   "id": 1,
   "ref": "45–49",
   "en": "'I truly believe that it was with the gods as our protectors, and with Juno's favour, that the Trojan ships held this course before the wind. What a city you will see rise here, sister, what a kingdom, from such a marriage! With the Trojans' arms marching beside our own, to what heights will Carthage's glory raise itself!",
   "en_marked": "'[I|4] [truly|2] [believe|4] that it was with [the gods|1] [as our protectors|3], [and|5] with [Juno's|6] [favour|7], that the [Trojan|10] [ships|13] [held|12] [this|8] [course|9] [before the wind|11]. [What a|14] [city|16] [you|15] [will see|19] [rise|21] [here|18], [sister|17], [what a|20] [kingdom|22], from [such|24] a [marriage|23]! With the [Trojans'|25] [arms|27] [marching beside|26] {our own|Not in the Latin. Added to make clear that the Trojan forces would fight alongside Carthage's own.}, [to what heights|30,33] [will|31] [Carthage's|28] [glory|32] [raise|31] [itself|29]!",
