 "context": [
  {
   "h": "Juno and Carthage",
   "body": "<p>Juno is Carthage's patron goddess and the great enemy of Aeneas and the Trojans throughout the <em>Aeneid</em>. She knows the Fates have decreed that Aeneas' descendants will found Rome and one day destroy Carthage, and she is determined to delay or prevent it. A marriage between Aeneas and Dido would keep him in Africa and away from Italy.</p><p>Virgil's Roman readers knew how the story ended: Rome and Carthage fought three Punic Wars, and Carthage was destroyed in 146 BC. Anna's vision of Punic glory rising with Trojan help is full of irony for them.</p>"
  }
